  "description": "The CTD data was obtained during leg #0603 of the 2006 ArcticNet scientific cruise. The data were collected from October 25 to 27, 2006, aboard the CCGS Amundsen. There were 21 CTD casts, associated to 18 oceanographic stations, in the Hudson Bay and Foxe Basin. The following parameters were measured: temperature, conductivity and pressure (with a Sea-Bird SBE-9plus), dissolved oxygen (Sea-Bird SBE-43), pH (Sea-Bird SBE-18-I), fluorescence (Seapoint chlorophyll fluorometer), nitrate concentration (Satlantic MBARI-ISUS 5T), transmittance (Wetlabs C-Star transmissiometer), light intensity (PAR; Biospherical Instruments QCP2300) and surface light intensity (sPAR; Biospherical Instruments QCP2200). Quality control procedures were applied to the data. Data are available on the Polar Data Catalogue and at the Marine Environmental Data Service (MEDS) of Fisheries and Oceans Canada.\ncdm_data_type=Profile\ncdm_profile_variables=filename,platform_name,platform_id,cruise_name,cruise_number,cast_number,station,time,latitude,longitude\ncomment=##Limitations:\nPurpose: The physical data are one of the tools used to characterize the water masses and, to some extent, the water circulation in the Hudson Bay and Foxe Basin.\n\n Supplemental Information: Summary: Not Applicable Research Program(s): ArcticNet. For further information: pdc@arcticnet.ulaval.ca\ncontributor_name=Yves, Gratton;Dany, Dumont;Marie-Emmanuelle, Rail;Annie, Simard;Stéphane, Thanassekos;ArcticNet;Amundsen Science;Amundsen Science\ncontributor_role=principalInvestigator,originator;collaborator;collaborator;collaborator;collaborator;pointOfContact,owner,distributor;owner,distributor;pointOfContact,custodian\nConventions=COARDS,ACDD-1.3,CF-1.6,CF-1.7,CF-1.8,CF-1.9\ndoi=https://doi.org/10.5884/509\nEasternmost_Easting=-75.8348\nfeatureType=Profile\ngeospatial_lat_max=67.8837\ngeospatial_lat_min=63.5352\ngeospatial_lat_units=degrees_north\ngeospatial_lon_max=-75.8348\ngeospatial_lon_min=-82.1352\ngeospatial_lon_units=degrees_east\ngeospatial_vertical_max=375.94323902465544\ngeospatial_vertical_min=1.9800019165374572\ngeospatial_vertical_positive=down\ngeospatial_vertical_units=m\nid=ccin-509\ninfoUrl=https://catalogue.hakai.org/dataset/ca-cioos_None\ninstitution=ArcticNet\nkeywords_vocabulary=CIOOS: CIOOS Essential Ocean Variables Vocabulary\nmax_depth_m=340.08\nmetadata_form=https://cioos-siooc.github.io/metadata-entry-form#/en/amundsen/c8GqCtwH6sZnf3HtZhCgkOsmtoh1/ccin-509\nmetadata_link=https://doi.org/10.5884/509\nmin_depth_m=2.64\nnaming_authority=ca.cioos\nNorthernmost_Northing=67.8837\noriginal_filename=CTD_2006003_116_1_DN.ODF\npdc_ccin=509\nplatform=ship\nplatform_vocabulary=https://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L06/current/\nprogress=completed\nproject=ArcticNet\nsounding_m=353\nsourceUrl=(local files)\nSouthernmost_Northing=63.5352\nstandard_name_vocabulary=CF Standard Name Table v79\nsubsetVariables=platform_name,platform_id,cruise_name,cruise_number,cast_number,station\ntime_coverage_end=2006-10-27T18:08:00Z\ntime_coverage_start=2006-10-25T09:09:00Z\nWesternmost_Easting=-82.1352",
